WebAssembly Core 2.0 SIMD128 conformance data

Repository: https://github.com/WebAssembly/spec
Revision: fffc6e12fa454e475455a7b58d3b5dc343980c10 (tag wg-2.0)

Cases.tsv contains 22,632 literal assert_return cases extracted from
 test/core/simd/*.wast. It is derived test data under Apache-2.0 (LICENSE).
The generator resolves simple exported operations and retains literal inputs,
expected bit patterns, expected NaN lanes and the original source filename.
It excludes compound expressions. For direct load cases it freezes the accessed
bytes of initialized memory into an input snapshot; the C++ adapter uses an
ordinary MIR address. Protection-page tests additionally check access widths.

Instructions.def lists all 236 standard 0xfd instructions from
 document/core/binary/instructions.rst. The source document is covered by the
W3C Software and Document Notice and License (DOCUMENT-LICENSE).
The numbers are inventory identifiers, never MIR protocol numbers.

Regenerate: python3 tests/SIMD/GenerateCases.py /path/to/pinned/spec
No network access, Wasm parser or code generation is used by normal builds.
